ABSTRACT_EN = [
    ("p", "We propose EGAT-MAPPO for joint channel assignment and routing in multi-hop Wi-Fi mesh networks. Every node is an agent that chooses its downlink channel and its parent. The model combines an edge-aware GATv2 encoder, two decision timescales and a residual prior from Ko's local-cost rule; it is warm-started by behaviour cloning, trained with MAPPO and executed in a decentralised way with switch hysteresis. In a 20-node, six-channel simulator whose airtime model is calibrated against ns-3, over 11 scenarios, we compare it with M0, Ko, Q-neutral, Yuan (GAT+DQN) and Li (GAT-A2C) on a five-metric composite fixed before the main experiments. On the test topologies its composite exceeds every adapted baseline by more than 10% (Ko +21.9%, Li +13.7%, Yuan +19.1%), and on fresh topologies it improves on Ko by 23.8%. Most of the gain over Ko comes from fewer switches (throughput +8.5%). With the same hysteresis it still beats Li (+5.7%) but ties Yuan (+0.7%). In ns-3 it significantly beats Li, Yuan and Li with hysteresis, while its gain over Ko (+10.7%) is not significant."),
    ("p", "Keywords  Channel assignment  Routing  Graph attention  MAPPO  Wi-Fi mesh"),
]

